        "subject": "LU-19431 tests: except sanity-pcc/40 for older clients",
        "message": "LU-19431 tests: except sanity-pcc/40 for older clients\n\nsanity-pcc test_40 would fail on 2.16 clients with \"Total time for\nasync open attach should be smaller\".  On these clients the open\nattach of the 50MB file with O_DIRECT fails with -EFAULT, because\nthe hybrid I/O switch makes the data copy into the PCC file use\ndirect I/O on a kernel buffer, so the 1G threshold read is served\nfrom the OSTs and is faster than the background attach.  This was\nfixed in the client for 2.17.0 by commit 0bff4700a977 (\"LU-19092\npcc: avoid hybrid I/O switch for PCC data copy\"), and newer\nclients pass the test against any server.\n\nAdd sanity-pcc.lu19431.ex to skip test_40 on clients before 2.17.0.\n\nAlso add the llite.pcc_async_threshold(4) man page.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-pcc\nTest-Parameters: testlist=sanity-pcc clientversion=2.16 env=ONLY=40,HONOR_EXCEPT=y\nSigned-off-by: Andreas Dilger <adilger@thelustrecollective.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5 ltvm llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I92be5b3b99be48b40f1107250ae96016403ebbe5\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
